"The preserved user report describes image-generation behaviour becoming active around image-related language or an uploaded image before a final explicit generation instruction. The report supports the observable interaction-state anomaly but does not identify the internal routing, tool-selection or control mechanism responsible.",
"The governance boundary is between conversational preparation and execution-bearing interaction state. Mentioning an image, discussing a prompt or uploading material for analysis does not necessarily mean 'generate now'. A well-governed multimodal interface should preserve whether the user is describing, analysing, preparing or authorising a transformation and should not silently carry an armed tool state across ambiguous turns.",
